-- ind-a-tests-readings.l4: the NON-DEFAULT readings of the forks of G1 to G4, each asserted on a discriminating scenario.
-- PROVENANCE, which differs from every other ind-a module: these expected values were decided at STEP 5, after the fork registers (FRAGMENT-G1 to G4) had been read
-- and after a probe had re-run ind-a's scenarios under each reading. Each value is what the TEXT gives when read the way the reading says (provision + reading -> value),
-- not what ind-a expects the Law to mean; where ind-a judges a reading untenable against the words, the comment says so ("reading misreads the text").
-- Readings already pinned in the other modules are not repeated (F1.1 B, F1.3 B on (g), F1.4 B, F2.1 B on 5(1)(a), F2.3 B on 5(2), F2.10 C, F3.1 B, F3.4 B, F3.5 B, F3.11 B, F4.1 B, F4.3 B, F4.6 B).

§ `ind-a tests: the other readings of the forks of Articles 1 to 12`

§§ `G1: Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`

-- F1.2 B ("only limb (i) is tied to the charity"): a dishonesty offence by any person, in relation to no charity, is misconduct. Reading misreads the text: the words "in relation [to] a registered charity ..." are in the lead-in of 2(10)(b) and govern every limb (src:111).
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` (`Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` WITH `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred` IS `not on the register`, `standing of the entity when the question is asked` IS `not on the register`, `the constitutional Laws of the charity` IS EMPTY, `an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS FALSE, `by the registered charity or by one of its governors` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE, `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE, `the offence is in relation to the entity` IS FALSE, `an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` IS FALSE, `an offence under the financial services Laws, any Regulation or Order made under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012` IS FALSE, `an offence under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007 or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS FALSE, `an offence under any other enactment relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS FALSE, `an offence under any other enactment or under customary law involving deception or dishonesty` IS TRUE, `an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey similar to one listed in (i) to (v)` IS FALSE) FALSE FALSE EMPTY

-- F1.3 B ("the enactment under which the body is incorporated"): a body within (h) has as its constitutional Law the UK Act under which it was incorporated (src:63, src:85).
#ASSERT `Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.3 read the other way` `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` `ind-a body under a UK Act` EQUALS JUST (`the enactment under which the body was incorporated` "Industrial and Provident Societies Act (extended)")

-- F1.5 B ("the likelihood of the manner, judged objectively"): published only if the manner is in fact likely to reach the audience. Reading misreads the text: src:30 says "in the opinion of the person publishing".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` (`Facts about a publication` WITH `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE, `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE, `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` (`Facts about a publication` WITH `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE, `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE, `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE)

-- F1.8 B ("(g) is the residue"): a foundation is within (d) only, an incorporated 1862 association within (c) only (my own expectation S2.1-08/09, which the default reading does not give: AMB-5, AMB-6).
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `ind-a Jersey foundation body` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `ind-a 1862 association` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`

§§ `G2: Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

`ind-a r no 6(2) facts` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`ind-a r pf` p MEANS `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH purpose IS p, facts IS `ind-a r no 6(2) facts`

GIVEN presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` presumed MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS presumed
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

`ind-a r no permissions` MEANS `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS EMPTY

GIVEN who IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
      acting IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`ind-a r governor may be` who acting MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH
        `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` WITH
                                                                        `what the constitution expressly permits` IS `any of the governors of the entity to be`
                                                                        `the person permitted` IS who
                                                                        `acting in that capacity` IS acting)

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
      cf IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      det IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a r meets` interp ps cf det MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` interp (`ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE EMPTY ps) (map `ind-a r pf` ps) cf `the Chief Minister` det FALSE

-- F2.1 B ("an entity with no purposes satisfies the test vacuously"): no purposes, public benefit found -> meets (src:146-149).
#ASSERT `ind-a r meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` EMPTY `ind-a r no permissions` (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` FALSE)
-- F2.1 C ("purely ancillary purposes satisfy the test without any charitable purpose"): ancillary trading only -> meets; no purposes -> meets.
#ASSERT `ind-a r meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` (LIST `ind-a ancillary trading purpose`) `ind-a r no permissions` (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-a r meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` EMPTY `ind-a r no permissions` (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` FALSE)
-- F2.2 B ("any such person is caught however the person is to act"): a States member permitted as governor in a private capacity -> does not meet. Reading misreads the text: src:154 "acting in that capacity".
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a r meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.2 read as B` (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`, `ind-a education purpose`) (`ind-a r governor may be` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` FALSE)
-- F2.3 B ("only the Minister, as Article 1 defines the term"): the Minister for Health permitted to be a governor, acting as such -> the test is met (src:151 with src:26).
#ASSERT `ind-a r meets` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`, `ind-a education purpose`) (`ind-a r governor may be` (`a Minister` NOTHING) TRUE) (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` FALSE)

`ind-a r days counted` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` OF `F2.1 A`, `F2.2 A`, `F2.3 A`, `F2.4 B`, `F2.5 A`, `F2.6 A`, `F2.7 A`, `F2.8 A`, `F2.9 A`, `F2.10 A`, `F2.11 A`, `F2.12 A`, `F2.13 A`, `F2.14 A`
`ind-a r days counted from the event day` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` OF `F2.1 A`, `F2.2 A`, `F2.3 A`, `F2.4 B`, `F2.5 A`, `F2.6 B`, `F2.7 A`, `F2.8 A`, `F2.9 A`, `F2.10 A`, `F2.11 A`, `F2.12 A`, `F2.13 A`, `F2.14 A`

-- F2.4 B ("a number of days counted from the event"): a copy provided 19 days after issue is in time with 30 days, not with 10 (src:164); laid 26 days after receipt: in time with 30, not with 20 (src:165).
#ASSERT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a r days counted` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 20)) FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a r days counted` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 20)) FALSE 10
#ASSERT `Art 5(8) the Minister laid the guidance and the report before the States in time` `ind-a r days counted` (YMD 2025 3 20) (JUST (YMD 2025 4 15)) FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(8) the Minister laid the guidance and the report before the States in time` `ind-a r days counted` (YMD 2025 3 20) (JUST (YMD 2025 4 15)) FALSE 20
-- F2.6 B with F2.4 B ("the day of the event is the first day"): a copy provided exactly 30 days after issue is in time on F2.6 A and late on F2.6 B.
#ASSERT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a r days counted` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 31)) FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a r days counted from the event day` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 31)) FALSE 30
-- F2.5 B ("paragraph (1)(c), as if the analogy made it religion"): humanism is within 6(1)(c). Reading misreads the text: src:194 says "for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p)".
#ASSERT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` `ind-a humanism purpose`
-- F2.7 ("before issuing or amending guidance"): consultation and report on the day the guidance is issued -> too late on A, in time on B (src:158).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.7 read as B` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))
-- F2.8 B ("each example is a power in its own right"): an example not conducive to any function -> still a power on B; not on A (src:133).
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.8 read as B` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` FALSE FALSE

GIVEN practicable IS A BOOLEAN, sought IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
`ind-a r limb` practicable sought MEANS `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` WITH `it appeared to the Commissioner to be reasonably practicable to act in that way` IS practicable, `the Commissioner sought to act in that way` IS sought

-- One limb appeared practicable and was not sought; another limb did not appear practicable.
`ind-a r conduct` MEANS
    `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` WITH
        `protects public trust and confidence in registered charities` IS `ind-a r limb` TRUE FALSE
        `is compatible with the encouragement of all forms of charitable giving` IS `ind-a r limb` FALSE FALSE
        `is compatible with the encouragement of voluntary participation in the work of registered charities` IS `ind-a r limb` TRUE TRUE
        `is proportionate as to the burdens imposed on registered charities` IS `ind-a r limb` TRUE TRUE
        `supports the development of registered charities` IS `ind-a r limb` TRUE TRUE

-- F2.9 ("so far as reasonably practicable"): limb by limb (A) the unsought practicable limb is a failure; whole way (B) the standard does not bind, since not every limb appeared practicable (src:137).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `ind-a r conduct`
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.9 read as B` `ind-a r conduct`
-- F2.10 B ("the finding of the determination stands"): the Commissioner presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit and found public benefit -> public benefit stands (src:211).
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` (`ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE EMPTY (LIST `ind-a education purpose`)) (`ind-a r Commissioner finds public benefit` TRUE)
-- F2.11 ("equality and diversity"): a purpose promoting equality but not diversity -> not (l) on A, (l) on B (src:179).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`ind-a purpose under` "equal pay advocacy" `the promotion of equality and diversity`) (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE, `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE, `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING, `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose promotes equality` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose promotes diversity` IS JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`ind-a purpose under` "equal pay advocacy" `the promotion of equality and diversity`) (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE, `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE, `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING, `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose promotes equality` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose promotes diversity` IS JUST FALSE)
-- F2.12 ("which guidance 5(6) to 5(8) apply to"): guidance on governors' duties alone -> not reached on A, reached on B (src:158 with src:128).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (LIST `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`)
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.12 read as B` (LIST `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`)

§§ `G3: Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

GIVEN start IS A `When the ten years of retention under Article 8(6) begin`
      year IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return`
      reach IS A `Reach of Article 10(4) to an entity that has been deregistered`
      counting IS A `Whether the day of an event is counted in a period of years`
      adding IS A `How a year is added to a date that does not exist in the target year`
      effect IS A `The day on which an entry in a section of the register takes effect`
      recent IS A `Which year is the most recent year`
      notices IS A `Which required steps notices Article 8(3)(k) notes`
      office IS A `Which entities fall within Article 8(4)(a)`
      dwelling IS A `What follows when the main premises are a private dwelling house`
      section IS A `The section that decides Article 8(5)(b)`
      who IS A `Who must meet a condition prescribed under Article 9(2)`
      ba IS A `Whether Article 8(3)(a) reaches sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1)`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
`ind-a r R` start year reach counting adding effect recent notices office dwelling section who ba MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
        `start of the ten years of retention` IS start
        `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS year
        `reach of Article 10(4)` IS reach
        `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS counting
        `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS adding
        `day on which an entry takes effect` IS effect
        `the most recent year` IS recent
        `required steps notices noted` IS notices
        `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS office
        `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS dwelling
        `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS section
        `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS who
        `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS ba

-- The favoured readings, by name, for building one-fork variants below.
`ind-a r R3 favoured` MEANS `ind-a r R` `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy` `the calendar year` `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary` `the date moves back to the last day of the month` `on the day of the entry` `the latest year that has ended before the day asked` `every notice that has been served` `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey` `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached` `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration` `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`
