        entity IS `ind-a r entity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`)
        `registration number` IS "JC-0042"
        `registered name` IS "Hope Jersey"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS reg
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the prevention or relief of poverty"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "relief of poverty in Jersey by a food bank"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

-- F3.1 C ("from the day the copy ceases to be operative"): a constitution superseded on 2022-01-01 may be discarded from 2032-01-02; one not superseded is kept while the charity is registered (src:249).
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a r R F3.1 C` (`Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`, `date received or made` IS YMD 2019 3 1, `date it ceased to be operative` IS JUST (YMD 2022 1 1)) (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2032 1 2)
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a r R F3.1 C` (`Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`, `date received or made` IS YMD 2019 3 1, `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING) (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
-- F3.4 B with S8.6-03: a copy received 2020-02-29, the event day counted: discard from 2030-02-28.
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a r R F3.4 B` (`Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH kind IS `an annual return of the charity`, `date received or made` IS YMD 2020 2 29, `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING) (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2030 2 28)

GIVEN fyEnd IS A MAYBE DATE
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
GIVETH A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
`ind-a r returns` fyEnd returns MEANS `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS fyEnd, `annual returns sent` IS returns

GIVEN lastDay IS A DATE, sent IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
`ind-a r return` lastDay sent MEANS `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH `last day of the year to which it relates` IS lastDay, `date sent` IS sent

-- F3.2 B ("the charity's own financial year"): a 30 June year-end; the return for the year to 2026-06-30 sent 2026-09-01; asked 2027-02-01 -> sent on B, not sent on A (calendar 2026) (src:234).
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `ind-a r R F3.2 B` (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (YMD 2027 2 1) (`ind-a r returns` (JUST (YMD 2019 6 30)) (LIST `ind-a r return` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 9 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `ind-a r R3 favoured` (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (YMD 2027 2 1) (`ind-a r returns` (JUST (YMD 2019 6 30)) (LIST `ind-a r return` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 9 1)))
-- F3.7 B ("the year in progress"): calendar years, asked 2026-06-30, return for 2025 sent -> sent on A (2025 is the most recent), not on B (2026 is).
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `ind-a r R3 favoured` (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (YMD 2026 6 30) (`ind-a r returns` NOTHING (LIST `ind-a r return` (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2026 3 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `ind-a r R F3.7 B` (`ind-a r charity registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (YMD 2026 6 30) (`ind-a r returns` NOTHING (LIST `ind-a r return` (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2026 3 1)))
-- F3.3 B: a historic-section entry is within 10(4)'s reach (my AMBIG-9 other reading) (src:296).
#ASSERT `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` `ind-a r R F3.3 B` (`ind-a r entity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` (LIST `a company`)) TRUE
-- F3.6 B ("the day after the entry"): entered in the general section on 2019-03-01, asked that day -> in it on A, in no section yet on B.
#ASSERT `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` `ind-a r R3 favoured` (LIST `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` WITH `the section` IS `the general section`, `date of the entry` IS YMD 2019 3 1) (YMD 2019 3 1) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` `ind-a r R F3.6 B` (LIST `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` WITH `the section` IS `the general section`, `date of the entry` IS YMD 2019 3 1) (YMD 2019 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING

`ind-a r complied RSN` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 1
        `steps to be taken by` IS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS TRUE

-- F3.8 B ("only a notice that has not been complied with"): a complied-with notice is not noted under (k). Reading adds a condition the text does not have: src:235 "if a required steps notice has been served".
#ASSERT null (`Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` `ind-a r R F3.8 B` (LIST `ind-a r complied RSN`))
-- F3.9 B ("every company and foundation"): a company whose constitutional Law is given as not requiring an office -> its registered office (my AMB-8 expectation).
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `ind-a r R F3.9 B` (`ind-a r entity` `an applicant for registration` (LIST `a company`)) (`Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE, `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS JUST "1 Bond Street, St Helier", `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING, `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS LIST "La Rue, St Ouen") EQUALS LIST "1 Bond Street, St Helier"
-- F3.10 B ("8(4)(b) applies and gives no address"): main premises a private dwelling -> no principal address at all. Reading misreads the text: 8(4)(c) "if neither sub-paragraph (a) nor (b) applies" is the fallback (src:241-242).
#ASSERT null (`Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `ind-a r R F3.10 B` (`ind-a r entity` `an applicant for registration` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`)) (`Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE, `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS NOTHING, `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS JUST (`Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` WITH address IS "La Rue, St Ouen", `in Jersey` IS TRUE, `a private dwelling house` IS TRUE, `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS TRUE), `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS LIST "La Rue, St Ouen"))
-- F3.12 B ("only an applicant"): a general-section charity meeting the funding condition may not request (src:260-262).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(2) the request for entry in the restricted section may be made` `ind-a r R F3.12 B` (`ind-a r entity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`)) TRUE FALSE
-- F3.13 B: a (ba) entity's note gets the "also within (a)?" statement (FALSE) and needs details (src:224-225).
#ASSERT (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` `ind-a r R F3.13 B` (`ind-a r entity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`)))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT NOT null ((`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` `ind-a r R F3.13 B` (`ind-a r entity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`)))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)

§§ `G4: Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`

GIVEN f1 IS A `How the twelve months preceding an application are counted`
      f2 IS A `Which day is the date of an application`
      f3 IS A `What an application that does not comply leads to`
      f4 IS A `How the duty to register meets the bars on granting the application`
      f5 IS A `Whether a formerly registered charity is another registered charity`
      f6 IS A `How a year is taken back from 29 February`
      f7 IS A `Which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares`
      f8 IS A `Whether a previous registered name is still one of the charity's registered names`
      f9 IS A `How the period for the Commissioner's decision is counted`
      f10 IS A `How reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance`
      f11 IS A `Which payees Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reaches`
      f12 IS A `How applies or should be applied is read in Article 11(4)(f)`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
`ind-a r K` f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9 f10 f11 f12 MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` WITH
        `how the twelve months preceding the application are counted` IS f1
        `which day is the date of the application` IS f2
        `what an application that does not comply leads to` IS f3
        `how the duty to register meets the bars on granting the application` IS f4
        `whether a formerly registered charity is another registered charity` IS f5
        `how a year is taken back from 29 February` IS f6
        `which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares` IS f7
        `whether a previous registered name is still one of its registered names` IS f8
        `how the period for the Commissioner's decision is counted` IS f9
        `how reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance` IS f10
        `which payees Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reaches` IS f11
        `how applies or should be applied is read in Article 11(4)(f)` IS f12

`ind-a r a1` MEANS `the twelve months ending on the day before the application`
`ind-a r a2` MEANS `the day the application is lodged`
`ind-a r a3` MEANS `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply`
`ind-a r a4` MEANS `a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register`
`ind-a r a5` MEANS `a formerly registered charity is not another registered charity`
`ind-a r a6` MEANS `a year before 29 February is 28 February`
`ind-a r a7` MEANS `its registered name and its alternative registered names`
`ind-a r a8` MEANS `a previous registered name is not one of its registered names`
`ind-a r a9` MEANS `the period starts the day after the date of the application`
`ind-a r a10` MEANS `as a determination the caller supplies`
`ind-a r a11` MEANS `a payee who was a governor when the payment was made`
`ind-a r a12` MEANS `a ground of mandatory refusal applies, or a ground of discretionary refusal should be applied`

`ind-a r K favoured` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.1 C` MEANS `ind-a r K` `the twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.2 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `the day the application becomes complete` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.3 C` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.4 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `the duty to register prevails once its six matters hold` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.4 C` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `the duty to register and the bars conflict and the model refuses` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.5 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `a formerly registered charity is another registered charity` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.7 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `its registered name only` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.7 C` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `every name entered for it in the register, previous names included` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.8 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `a previous registered name is still one of its registered names` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.9 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `the date of the application is the first day of the period` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.10 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `as a number of days from the event` `ind-a r a11` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.11 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `a payee who is a governor on the date of the application` `ind-a r a12`
`ind-a r K F4.12 B` MEANS `ind-a r K` `ind-a r a1` `ind-a r a2` `ind-a r a3` `ind-a r a4` `ind-a r a5` `ind-a r a6` `ind-a r a7` `ind-a r a8` `ind-a r a9` `ind-a r a10` `ind-a r a11` `any prescribed ground whose circumstances are present defeats the matter`

`ind-a r info` MEANS `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH `provided as at the time of the application` IS TRUE, `would differ once the entity is registered` IS FALSE, `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS FALSE

GIVEN lodged IS A DATE
      complete IS A MAYBE DATE
      payments IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor`
GIVETH AN `Application for registration`
`ind-a r application` lodged complete payments MEANS
    `Application for registration` WITH
        dates IS `Dates of an application` WITH `date lodged` IS lodged, `date on which it became complete` IS complete
        `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `Particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH
            `how the applicant meets Article 11(4)(c) and (d)` IS `ind-a r info`
            `matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)` IS `ind-a r info`
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant` IS FALSE
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)` IS `ind-a r info`
        `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` WITH
            `copy of the applicant's constitution` IS TRUE
            `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` IS TRUE
            `draft of the registered public benefit statement` IS TRUE
        `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `Financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` WITH
            `most recent financial accounts exist` IS FALSE
            `details of the most recent financial accounts` IS FALSE
            `payments made to governors` IS payments
            `payments to governors disclosed in the application` IS EMPTY
            `draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE
            `Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 would require other financial information` IS FALSE
            `other financial information required under that Law` IS FALSE
            `entry in the restricted section is requested` IS FALSE
            `Order prescribes further financial information` IS FALSE
            `further financial information prescribed by Order` IS FALSE
        `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `Other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` WITH
            `Regulations under Article 11(3) require other information, documents or evidence` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations` IS FALSE
            `procedure under Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) followed` IS TRUE
            `Commissioner has requested other information, documents or evidence to determine the application` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner` IS FALSE
        `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

`ind-a r applicant` MEANS `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey" `an applicant for registration` (LIST `a company`) TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`)

GIVEN willMeet IS A BOOLEAN, written IS A BOOLEAN, mayPresent IS A BOOLEAN, mayApplied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
`ind-a r findings` willMeet written mayPresent mayApplied MEANS
    `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` WITH
        `applicant will meet the charity test on registration` IS willMeet
        `constitution of the applicant is a written document` IS written
        `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS FALSE
        `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present` IS mayPresent
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` IS mayApplied

GIVEN k IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
      c195 IS A BOOLEAN
      findings IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
      bar199 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
`ind-a r duty` k c195 findings bar199 MEANS
    `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` k (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) FALSE c195 `ind-a r applicant` TRUE findings TRUE FALSE bar199 FALSE

GIVEN k IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
      lodged IS A DATE
      complete IS A MAYBE DATE
      paid IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a r in window` k lodged complete paid MEANS `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` k (`ind-a r application` lodged complete EMPTY) paid

-- F4.1 C ("twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application"): application 2025-03-15 -> the window is 2024-03-01 to 2025-02-28 (src:310).
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `ind-a r K F4.1 C` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2024 3 1), (YMD 2025 2 28)
#ASSERT `ind-a r in window` `ind-a r K F4.1 C` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) (YMD 2024 3 14)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a r in window` `ind-a r K F4.1 C` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) (YMD 2025 3 14)
-- F4.2 B ("the day the application becomes complete"): lodged 2025-03-15, complete 2025-04-01 -> a payment on 2025-03-20 is inside on B, outside on A; an application never completed has no date on B.
#ASSERT `ind-a r in window` `ind-a r K F4.2 B` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) (YMD 2025 3 20)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a r in window` `ind-a r K favoured` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) (YMD 2025 3 20)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11 the date of the application` `ind-a r K F4.2 B` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) NOTHING EMPTY)
-- F4.3 C ("the duty to refuse depends on the six matters alone"): a non-complying application whose matters fail (unwritten constitution) -> must refuse on C; no duty on A (src:328).
#ASSERT `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K F4.3 C` FALSE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K favoured` FALSE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
-- F4.4 ("the duty to register meets the bars"): complies, six matters found, an undetermined fitness issue (19(9)(c)) -> A must not yet grant; B must register; C refuses (src:502).
#ASSERT `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K favoured` TRUE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
#ASSERT `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K F4.4 B` TRUE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K F4.4 C` TRUE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
-- F4.12 B ("any prescribed ground whose circumstances are present defeats the matter"): a discretionary ground present that the Commissioner would not apply -> must refuse on B (src:327).
#ASSERT `ind-a r duty` `ind-a r K F4.12 B` TRUE (`ind-a r findings` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `Name entered in the register`
GIVETH A `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
`ind-a r opinion on` entries MEANS
    `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` WITH
        `name in question` IS "Jersey Hope"
        `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name` IS entries
        `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IS FALSE
        `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IS FALSE
        `offensive` IS FALSE

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register`
      st IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A `Name entered in the register`
`ind-a r other charity's` kind st MEANS `Name entered in the register` WITH name IS "Jersey Hope", `kind of entry` IS kind, `standing of the entity that holds it` IS st, `held by the entity itself` IS FALSE

-- F4.5 B: the same as a deregistered charity's former name -> undesirable. Reading misreads the defined term: src:34 "registered charity" is an entity entered in the general or restricted section.
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a r K F4.5 B` (`ind-a r opinion on` (LIST `ind-a r other charity's` `the registered name` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`))
-- F4.7 ("which names of another charity"): another charity's alternative registered name -> counted on A, not on B; another charity's previous name -> counted on C only (src:355).
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a r K favoured` (`ind-a r opinion on` (LIST `ind-a r other charity's` `an alternative registered name` `entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a r K F4.7 B` (`ind-a r opinion on` (LIST `ind-a r other charity's` `an alternative registered name` `entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a r K favoured` (`ind-a r opinion on` (LIST `ind-a r other charity's` `a previous registered name` `entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a r K F4.7 C` (`ind-a r opinion on` (LIST `ind-a r other charity's` `a previous registered name` `entered in the general section`))

`ind-a r Hope` MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`)
        `registration number` IS "JC-0042"
        `registered name` IS "Hope Jersey"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2025 5 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the prevention or relief of poverty"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "relief of poverty in Jersey by a food bank"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

`ind-a r using the old name` MEANS
    `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
        `name used` IS "Hope for Jersey"
        `previous registered names of the charity` IS LIST "Hope for Jersey"
        `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS FALSE
        `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

-- F4.8 ("a previous registered name"): the charity uses its own former registered name, not otherwise related -> prohibited on A, permitted on B (src:367).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `ind-a r K favoured` `ind-a r Hope` `ind-a r using the old name`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `ind-a r K F4.8 B` `ind-a r Hope` `ind-a r using the old name`
-- F4.9 ("counting the decision period"): lodged 2025-03-15, an Order of 30 days -> last day 2025-04-14 on A, 2025-04-13 on B (src:339).
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `ind-a r K favoured` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `ind-a r K F4.9 B` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 13
-- F4.10 B ("a number of days from the event"): a copy provided 20 days after issue is in time with 30 days; with no number given there is no answer (src:164 via src:331).
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `ind-a r K F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 21) (JUST 30)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `ind-a r K F4.10 B` FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 21) NOTHING

`ind-a r payment to a former governor` MEANS `Payment to a governor` WITH `name of the payee` IS "Guy Mauger", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2024 6 1, `amount paid` IS 500, `payee was a governor when the payment was made` IS TRUE, `payee is a governor on the date of the application` IS FALSE

-- F4.11 ("a governor when?"): a payment in the window to a person who was a governor when paid but is not one at the application -> reached on A, not on B (src:310).
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `ind-a r K favoured` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) `ind-a r payment to a former governor`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `ind-a r K F4.11 B` (`ind-a r application` (YMD 2025 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 15)) EMPTY) `ind-a r payment to a former governor`
